course: dictionary
lesson: 10817
title: Vegan and diet words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a noun or an adjective, and the sentence tells you which. «Vegans eat no food from animals at all.» Here vegans are people, so it is a noun. «Vegan food» describes the food, so vegan is an adjective.
explain: Context clues help you work out the meaning. «Vegetarians eat no meat or fish, and vegans eat no food from animals at all.» The word «and» and the phrase «at all» show that vegans avoid more animal foods than vegetarians do. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Be kind when you talk about diets. «People are vegetarian or vegan for health, belief or love of animals, so never try to make them eat meat.» People have different reasons for their choices, and respecting them is good manners.
fact: A vegan is a person who eats no food from animals at all.
fact: Vegan, as an adjective, means containing no animal products, as in «a vegan cake».
fact: Vegans eat no meat, fish, milk, cheese, eggs or honey.
fact: Vegetarians eat no meat or fish.
fact: Vegans eat fruit, vegetables, grains, beans, nuts and seeds.
fact: «Vegan» can be a noun when it names a person, and an adjective when it describes something.
exercise: «Vegans eat no food from animals at all.» What is a vegan? | *A person who eats no food from animals at all | A person who eats only meat | A person who grows vegetables only at home | A person who eats fish on Fridays
exercise: Which food is vegan? | *Fruit, beans and nuts | Fish and chips | A cheese sandwich | Honey on toast
exercise: «Vegetarians eat no meat or fish, and vegans eat no food from animals at all.» Which is true? | Vegetarians and vegans both eat chicken | Vegans eat fish but vegetarians do not | Vegetarians avoid more animal foods than vegans do | *Vegans avoid more animal foods than vegetarians do
test: Why is it good manners to respect someone's diet? | Everyone must eat meat to be polite | Vegans cannot eat fruit | *People choose diets for different reasons, so their choice deserves respect | Vegan food is always tasteless
test: «Vegans usually need a B12 supplement, an extra pill, because B12 comes mainly from animal foods.» Why might a vegan need a pill? | Vegans cannot eat any vitamins | Pills taste nice | *Because B12 comes mainly from animal foods | Because animal foods have no energy
exam: «Many Hindus and Buddhists are vegetarian because their faiths teach care for animal life.» What is one reason some people choose a vegetarian diet? | Vegetables are against the law | They dislike fruit | Meat is too expensive for everyone | *Their religion teaches care for animal life
